// Demonstrates that `count where φ` counts occurrences (distinct
// tps), not distinct values. This trace has the user re-reading the
// same document repeatedly; an equivalent `count d where Read(...,
// document: d)` would top out at the number of distinct documents
// (1), so the rate limit would never engage. With `count where`
// every Read tp counts separately, so the limit kicks in.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
